(Z ZERO: TOP OF THE SPOILBOARD {touch plate on the board})
(XY ZERO: the front-left corner of the area, 0.25 in in from the front-left limits of travel: jog to)
(the front-left limit of X and Y travel, move 0.25 in towards the back and 0.25 in to the right, then)
(zero X and Y.)
(WHOLE BED: the bit's centre stays 0.25 in inside the travel's limits on every side, so it surfaces)
(62.125 x 62.125 in: the area plus the bit's radius all round. Any of the board beyond that isn't)
(surfaced.)
(NATIVECAM SPOILBOARD SURFACING: 60.875 x 60.875 in, 1 pass of 0.02 in {0.02 in in all} with 1-1/4in)
(Surfacing Bit, 99 lines along X 0.621 in apart, both ways.)
(BED CLEAR: remove every clamp. Every screw head and T-nut must sit at least 0.125 in below the cut.)
(Set the dust shoe high enough for the surfacing bit's collet and the 0.5 in clearance.)
(Re-zero Z on the board before every run: each run takes 0.02 in off the surface it is zeroed on.)
(Runs about 41 min.)
(NativeCAM spoilboard surfacing)
